The full legal code is available at:

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/legalcode

A human-readable summary is at:

    https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/

THE SPECIFICATION IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND.

---

Why this is CC0 and the rest of the project is not:

The Animus Live application source is licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0. The file
format is deliberately separated and placed in the public domain so that
anyone can implement a reader or writer for `.animus` projects with zero
legal analysis and no obligation to this project — including in proprietary
software, and including in a competing tool.

A creative tool's project format is the user's data, not the vendor's. A
performer's show should outlive the program that made it.

The reference implementation of this format lives in the `animus-core` and
`animus-project` crates and remains MIT OR Apache-2.0, so implementers may
also simply vendor the Rust code rather than working from the prose.
